# Incident notes for the 2026-06 evaluation sweep

**INC-4471 - evaluation sink outage (workers w03, w07).**  Between 2026-06-27T00:00:00Z and
2026-07-03T12:00:00Z the primary results writer on workers w03 and w07 dropped its connection.  Runs that
*started* in that window on those two workers did not get a row in `eval_results.csv`.  The failure was in
the writer, not in the evaluation: it does not depend in any way on what the run scored.

Some of those values were later scraped out of the per-worker stdout tails and are kept under
`recovered/`, one shard per collection pass, in percent units.  The scrape was opportunistic:

  * it also re-captured runs whose primary row was fine, so a run can appear in both places;
  * it also captured runs whose row had already been removed by the retention sweep;
  * the shards were assembled from planning tickets, so they contain a few run ids for runs that were
    never launched at all, and a few rows appear twice.

Where a run appears more than once the values agree; treat the shards as a value source, never as a run
list.

**Retention sweep.**  Independently of the outage, a nightly job deletes result rows that fall under the
quality floor in force at the time it runs; the deletions are listed in `retention_log.csv` with reason
`below_retention_floor`, and the floors are versioned in `retention_policy.json`.  The same log also
records deletions the on-call operator made by hand to free disk space (`operator_disk_cleanup`); those
were chosen by age, not by score.

**Not affected.**  `plan.csv`, `launch_log.csv` and `retention_log.csv` are complete for the whole sweep.
